    "fidelity": "not-applicable",
    "note": "The finished design was read from Brian Wichmann’s FE1 drawing, its corners snapped to exact values. We devised the construction. It is the eight-fold star and cross: stars of two squares stand round O, every side carried on, and the lines through W add the next stars. Round O and round the tile’s corners the lines between the cross and its four stars are left out, so they make one large piece. The drawing gives no steps.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. The comparison with the drawing checks the finished lines, not how the design was first laid out. No photo of the ceiling was checked.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-26"
  },
  "credits": [
    {
      "source": "Tiling Search, data208/FE1: French Embassy, Cairo",
      "creator": "Brian Wichmann",
      "url": "https://tilingsearch.mit.edu/HTML/data208/FE1.html",
      "kind": "drawing",
      "note": "The design was read from his drawing. He takes it from Mercedes Volait, Maisons de France au Caire (Cairo, 2012), page 55, plate 38 (a ceiling of the French Embassy, Cairo). The construction is ours."
    }
